			"notes": "# Features\n* Most notably, added a new config option `require_link_to_play`, which restricts access to the world for players without linked accounts (and prompts them to do so).\n* Merged `send_player_joins` and `send_player_leaves` into `send_player_connections`.\n* Removed blacklisting text to send from Minecraft to Discord and vice-versa.\n* You can now show the currently running world's name using `{world}` in the `start_message` setting.\n* Configuration is now stored as JSON5, adding comments inside the file. You will need to bring over your settings from the old file to the new file manually.\n\n# Underlying changes\nA lot of everything was reorganized and rewritten for other dependencies that I found more pleasant to use.\n\n* Switched development from Java to Kotlin 2.0.\n* Switched the Discord library from JDA to Kord.\n* Switched the configuration from my own to Yet Another Config Lib.\n\nThis means that running this mod will now require Fabric Language Kotlin and Yet Another Config Lib installed on the server."
		},
